.\" The macros used below are those described in groff_man(7) and
 \" groff_man_style(7).
.
.TH guile\-config 1 "2025-12-12" "@GUILE_VERSION@" "GNU Guile"
.
.SH NAME
guile\-config \- a tool to retrieve Guile configuration information
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY guile-config
.B \-\-version
.YS
.SY guile-config
.B \-\-help
.RB [ SUBCOMMAND ]
.YS
.SY guile-config
.B link
.YS
.SY guile-config
.B compile
.YS
.SY guile-config
.BI info \ VAR
.YS
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B guile-config
reports configuration information for guile, including compilation and
linkage flags, and
.B pkg-config
variables.
.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B compile
Print C compiler flags for compiling code that uses Guile.  This
includes any
.B -I
flags needed to find Guile's header files.
.TP
.B link
Print linker flags for building the
.B guile
executable.  Print the linker command-line flags necessary to link
against the Guile library, and any other libraries it requires.
.TP
.BI info \ VAR
Display the value of the
.B pkg-config
variable
.I VAR
used when Guile was built.  Use this command to find out where Guile was
installed, where it will look for Scheme code at run-time, and so on.
.
.SH SEE ALSO
.
.IR guile (1),
.IR pkg-config (1),
and for much more detail, the
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/guile/manual/html_node/index.html
Guile Reference Manual
.UE
which may also be available via
.BR info\ guile
or
.B M\-x info
in emacs.
